  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MidEuropa VI</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Fund seeks to increase access to PE capital and value-creation for mid-market companies in Poland and the CEE region. Despite benefiting from developed financial institutions and EU capital markets, companies in Poland and other CEE countries have seen a decline in equity availability in recent years. The Fund will provide equity financing and create value to portfolio companies through buy &amp; build initiatives, operational improvements, talent hiring, digital transformation, and international expansion, leveraging its regional experience and strong local networks. Beyond the Project, IFC expects that the successful raising of this fund will help sustain PE market activity and signal confidence among regional funds, reinforcing commercial investor participation.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed transaction is an equity investment of up to 50 million to MidEuropa Fund VI SCSp (MidEuropa VI or the Fund). The Fund is a closed-end private equity (PE) fund to be domiciled in Luxembourg with a target size of 800 million. MidEuropa VI will target mid-market companies in Poland and other countries in Central and Eastern Europe (CEE).</narrative>
  </description>
